From: Andrzej Perczak <linux@andrzejperczak.com>
Subject: [PATCH] alarmtimer: minimize suspend wakeup timeout on android16-6.12.69

Alarmtimer sets a fixed 2 second wakeup timeout on suspend abort (-EBUSY)
regardless of the actual time remaining until the nearest timer expires.
Use ktime_to_ms(min) + 1 ms instead so the device can re-enter suspend as
soon as the pending alarm fires.

Signed-off-by: Andrzej Perczak <linux@andrzejperczak.com>
---
diff --git a/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c b/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c
index 8bf8886..e1fcb28 100644
--- a/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c
+++ b/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c
@@ -280,7 +280,7 @@ static int alarmtimer_suspend(struct device *dev)
 		return 0;
 
 	if (ktime_to_ns(min) < 2 * NSEC_PER_SEC) {
-		pm_wakeup_event(dev, 2 * MSEC_PER_SEC);
+		pm_wakeup_event(dev, ktime_to_ms(min) + 1);
 		return -EBUSY;
 	}
 
